# Spec 08 Phase A — post-move check-in (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before edits)
# A1 GIVEN a catalog task with surfaceAfterDaysPastMove = 1 and a move date,
#    WHEN a new frozen dose is computed before moveDate + 1 day, THEN that task
#    is absent and does not inflate the regular target; WHEN computed on or
#    after the gate, THEN it joins the dose under the ordinary urgency ordering.
# A2 GIVEN MOVE_CHECKIN and BOX_RETURN catalog rows, WHEN catalog validation and
#    the sanctioned reseed run, THEN MOVE_CHECKIN is unconditional at move + 1,
#    BOX_RETURN is gated to an existing supplies_kit workflow response at move
#    + 7, all fields round-trip, and no retired catalog/definition ghosts remain.
# A3 GIVEN a signed-in user with a book_movers response, WHEN move_checkin opens,
#    THEN the vendor-specific branch renders all four LOCKED factual yes/no
#    questions plus one optional note; GIVEN no booking response, THEN the
#    general branch renders the same factual form without inventing a vendor.
# A4 GIVEN all four answers, WHEN the user submits a flagged vendor response,
#    THEN submitCheckIn writes one backend-owned vendorReviews document with
#    vendorId, userId, answers, flags, and submittedAt and emits either the exact
#    PEEZY FLAG SMS family or the exact "SMS notify not configured" log; WHEN the
#    general path submits, THEN the stored vendorId is null.
# A5 GIVEN the Phase A diff, WHEN focused Swift/Node tests, syntax checks,
#    catalog validation, a fresh-context validator, and the exact iPhone 17 Pro
#    simulator build run, THEN every criterion receives evidence-backed PASS or
#    FAIL before the separate Phase A commit and only submitCheckIn plus the
#    catalog reseed are deployed.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - "Kit purchasers" is evaluated from the durable client-readable
#   users/{uid}/workflowResponses/supplies_kit document. A successful kit order
#   invokes the existing add-only generation refresh so BOX_RETURN is created
#   without overwriting any live task status.
# - "Any negative answer" means an adverse outcome: no for arrival/steady crew,
#   yes for over-quote cost/damage. Flags use stable machine ids and SMS uses the
#   corresponding factual label.
# - Post-move gating is a daily-dose surfacing rule. The full Tasks tab remains
#   the complete plan, matching its existing role; frozen-dose membership is
#   the acceptance surface named by the spec.
#
